# Generated output. Do not commit these directories.
#
# This project writes all of its output into a CMake build tree. That tree
# holds the CMake cache, the Nim cache, the generated C files, the object
# files, the static library and the CTest data. No build step writes into
# the source directories.
#
# Each rule starts with a slash. The slash limits the rule to the top
# directory of the repository, which is where CMake makes each tree.

# The default build tree. The README section "How to build" gives this
# command:
#   cmake -S . -B build
# The continuous integration job build-and-t0 uses the same name.
# cmake/Nim.cmake puts the Nim cache in this tree. It sets the cache to
# ${PROJECT_BINARY_DIR}/nimcache at configure time.
/build/

# The sanitizer build tree. The continuous integration job sanitizer-t0
# makes a second tree with this command:
#   cmake -S . -B build-asan
# A contributor who runs that job on a local machine makes the same tree.
/build-asan/

# This file lists the output of this project only. Keep editor files,
# operating system files and other personal files in your own global
# excludes file. Do not add them here.
